{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The prebuilt fused path is not numerically reliable with ordinary unshuffled weights in this environment, so I’m switching to a correctness-preserving dense-padded batched GEMM design: routes are stably grouped by expert, each of the three BF16 projections remains a separate rounded GEMM, and results are accumulated in the reference order. This removes 128 Python-dispatched expert loops without changing the math."}}
